RFC 5545 recurrence rule examples

Source: RFC 5545, "Internet Calendaring and Scheduling Core Object Specification
(iCalendar)", B. Desruisseaux, Ed., September 2009, section 3.8.5.3.
URL: https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5545#section-3.8.5.3

cases.json contains the DTSTART, EXDATE and RRULE lines of the examples in
section 3.8.5.3 and the instances that the example prose gives. Changes:
- The prose instances are written as local date-times with the UTC offset
  that the prose gives (EDT = -0400, EST = -0500).
- Lists that the prose shortens with "..." are expanded.
- Verified erratum 3883 (https://www.rfc-editor.org/errata/eid3883) is
  applied to the HOURLY example: UNTIL=19970902T210000Z.
tools/extract_rfc5545.py makes the file, and tools/verify_rfc5545.py checks it.

RFC 5545 also contains material from documents published before
November 10, 2008 (RFC 2445). Most of the examples come from RFC 2445.

